From 7071713eda050dcf3ad07545d1c2eb03e10050f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:06:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn device geometry: one reading from the DeviceProfile,
 in every state

launcher.device_profile no longer measures the launcher's views, with a
second, approximate sum when they are not laid out (just after an update,
the phone locked, no launcher activity yet). It reports the portrait
home screen's DeviceProfile - the object the Launcher activity lays out
with - put through the same sums Workspace, CellLayout,
ShortcutAndWidgetContainer and Hotseat make, so the reading is the same
in every state. The old fallback took Launcher3's visual cellWidthPx for
the layout cell and the full screen width for the dock, which squeezed
the desktop preview's grid (w 0.7167 of the screen instead of 0.9583).
The source field is gone with the second path, and so is the page
indicator (the preview never draws it).

The debug build's provider gets debug_home_views, which reads the views
back for the device test that checks the two agree.
---
